# ah_barnacles — "Ah, Barnacles" (Quest 7)
#
# The Mad Fisherman knows where Ralph and Sanjeet are and will not say so for free. Ten bus
# barnacles buys the answer: East York, and a pointer at Alex back in London.
#
# GRANTED BY: the Trap Branch Manager's post-defeat choice (quests/gangbusters.quest, node
# tbm_beaten), the same choice that completes Quest 6.
# COMPLETED BY: the Mad Fisherman's closing choice below, node mf_alex.
#
# Quest 8 ("Rush Hour") is TBC, so no GRANT of it is wired on that closing choice yet — the same
# shape wtf_mosley carried until Quest 6 existed.
#
# ⚠ NEW KEY: mad_fisherman (QuestActor). No item is new — bus_station_barnacles already exists and
# is already used by investigate_weird_vape.
#
# ⚠ THE BARNACLES ARE SHARED WITH QUEST 4. investigate_weird_vape collects 2 of this exact item and
# does NOT consume them, so a player arriving here still carrying that pair starts this stage at
# 2/10 rather than 0/10. Collect counts what is in the bag, not what was picked up for this quest.
# Deliberate to leave as-is — flagged so it is not mistaken for a miscount later.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS THE MAD FISHERMAN'S CONVERSATION — inline because he appears in no other quest.
# If Quest 8 gives him more to say, move the whole DIALOGUE block to
# quests/dialogue/madfisherman.quest first.

QUEST ah_barnacles
TITLE: Ah, Barnacles
GIVER: Trap Branch Manager
LOCATION: East of London.

# Stage 0 — a deliberately rough pointer: the owner's brief is that the journal names the chunk to
# the right of London and nothing more. Intermediate TalkTo, so it advances on the interact.
STAGE TALKTO mad_fisherman
OBJECTIVE: Find the Mad Fisherman.

# Stage 1 (last) — the gather. Ten single-item containers in the bus station chunk; a Collect stage
# never completes the quest itself, so the hand-in is the dialogue below.
STAGE COLLECT bus_station_barnacles x10
OBJECTIVE: Try going back to the abandoned bus station. Maybe next door is open now.
WHENMET: Sort out the Mad Fisherman with his barnacles.

REWARD
POUNDS: 50
XP: 120

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DIALOGUE madfisherman

NODE start
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: Arrr. What do you want?
CHOICE Have you heard of Ralph and Sanjeet? Croydon Spartans? -> mf_barnacle
GATE: stage ah_barnacles 0
# Greys out until all ten are carried, and takes them on the pick. Remove `consume` if he should
# only ever be shown them — the owner's script reads as a payment, so they are taken.
CHOICE There's the slimy bastards. Enjoy. -> mf_return
GATE: stage ah_barnacles 1
ITEM: bus_station_barnacles x10 consume
CHOICE End Conversation.

NODE mf_barnacle
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: Tha's ye fellas. Yarr. Good barnacle hunters they are.
CHOICE Can you tell me where they're staying at the minute? -> mf_laugh

NODE mf_laugh
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: *The Mad Fisherman laughs maniacally.*
# The owner's script has the player speechless here — "[...]" is verbatim, not a placeholder.
CHOICE [...] -> mf_owt

NODE mf_owt
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: Owt for nowt, you lot. Gen Deers or whatever.
CHOICE Well— -> mf_price

NODE mf_price
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: Ten bus barnacles, and I can help you.
# Ends the conversation. Stage 0 has already advanced on the interact, so the journal reads
# "Try going back to the abandoned bus station" as the chat closes.
CHOICE Brilliant. Bus barnacles again. Okay, I'll be back.

NODE mf_return
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: Arr, very nice there, lad. I knew you'd come back for me. Here's a little thing for you.
CHOICE Great, cheers. -> mf_eastyork

NODE mf_eastyork
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: So, all I can tell you is that Ralph and Sanjeet, they're staying in East York at the minute. I know the Chinese are keeping them there nice and cushy.
CHOICE Okay, right. I'll see what's up. -> mf_alex

NODE mf_alex
SPEAKER: madfisherman
SPEAK: Before you get going though, have a chat with Alex at his place in London. He's not very handy but the lad's cheap and willing back ya for a couple quid.
# Ends the chat, completes the quest (paying the £50 and 120 XP) and grants Quest 8 — the same
# shape as gangbusters' hand-off into this one. Granting rush_hour here is also what unlocks Alex:
# his conversation offers nothing but a greeting until this quest id exists and is active.
CHOICE Sounds good.
COMPLETE: ah_barnacles
GRANT: rush_hour
